ck to the super  bowl maybe going to another super bowl  is what what also counts because yeah  you know favre went to another super  bowl and  breeze having to get back to another  super bowl will mean a lot more  i i think that that the saints uh and  i'd love to se obviously it's impossible  to answer this question but if that  bounty gate baloney that the nfl trotted  out in 2012 at a time when plenty of  teams were doing the same thing but they  decided that they were going to change  the culture of the nfl as it relates to  bounties by finding one team that they  were going to hammer instead of putting  everyone on notice that hey you end the  bounties or we're going to hammer you  they found the saints they nailed the  saints they gutted the team from a  coaching standpoint a defense standpoint  in 2012 and it took them years to decor  to recover on the defensive side of the  ball meanwhile they're still hovering  around seven and nine eight and eight  every year  with abysmally bad defenses  and and and i i just i'd love to know  how competitive the saints would have  continued to be if they didn't have to  deal with that lost season of 2012  because 2011 remember that epic playoff  game against the 49ers i mean they were  still a team that was hanging around at  the top of the nfl and i think they  would have been more competitive they  would have more playoff appearances if  they didn't have to deal with 2012 in  the aftermath of it and i think bree's  presence and his skills kept that team  from spiraling out of control  yeah it's a good point it's a big time  what if that we will always get to play  and uh i i think if drew brees goes to  the super bowl he'll get that victory  lap that we're kind of talking about  where the media comes out and says you  know this guy's legacy it felt like it  was going to happen last year when you  had a little bit of mvp conversation  then he fell off towards the end of the  year the rams obviously come into the  superd